const glossary={
 'PowerEdge':'Dell’s server family. The complete model name identifies a particular hardware platform, not a universal set of options.',
 'R / T / MX / XR / XE':'Useful family cues: rack, tower, MX modular, edge / ruggedized and specialized accelerated systems. Confirm the complete model instead of treating a prefix as a specification.',
 '16G / 17G':'Dell server generations, separate from Intel / AMD CPU generations. A 17G PowerEdge can use Intel Xeon 6 or AMD EPYC 9005.',
 'Socket / 1P / 2P':'A socket holds a host processor. 1P and 2P mean one- and two-processor platforms. Core count is a different quantity.',
 'U versus OU':'A conventional rack unit (U) is 44.45 mm tall. An Open Rack Unit (OU) is 48 mm. XE9785L is an Open Rack v3 node; rack width, power and cooling matter too.',
 'EPYC 9005':'AMD’s 5th-generation EPYC CPU family. A server qualifies a subset of processor SKUs and operating limits.',
 'Xeon 6 / Xeon Scalable':'Intel CPU family names. Xeon 6 P-core / E-core offerings and earlier 4th / 5th Gen Xeon Scalable options are distinct platform qualifications.',
 'DIMM / DDR5':'A DIMM is a physical memory module. DDR5 is its memory technology. Slot count is not channel count, and memory speed depends on population.',
 'SFF / LFF':'Drive-size categories, usually 2.5-inch and 3.5-inch respectively. Size alone does not establish SAS, SATA or NVMe compatibility.',
 'SAS / SATA':'Interfaces used by supported hard disks and SSDs. Correct controllers, cables, carriers and backplanes are required.',
 'NVMe / U.2':'NVMe is a storage protocol commonly carried over PCIe. U.2 identifies a connector / drive implementation commonly used for 2.5-inch enterprise NVMe SSDs.',
 'EDSFF / E3.S / E1.S':'Enterprise flash form factors. E3.S and E1.S are physically different and require matching bays and cooling.',
 'M.2 / BOSS':'M.2 is a small storage-module shape. Dell’s Boot Optimized Storage Subsystem can provide dedicated boot SSDs with model-specific RAID options.',
 'PERC / HBA':'PowerEdge RAID Controller manages supported drive arrays. A host bus adapter supplies storage connectivity with a different role. NVMe is not automatically incompatible with hardware RAID.',
 'RAID':'A layout combining drives for performance or resilience. Usable capacity depends on the layout, and RAID is not a substitute for backup.',
 'PCIe / OCP NIC':'PCI Express connects expansion devices. An OCP NIC is a network card in an industry-standard server-adapter form factor.',
 'iDRAC':'Integrated Dell Remote Access Controller: individual-server management independent of the workload operating system. Check generation, license and firmware.',
 'OpenManage Enterprise':'A console for inventory, monitoring and supported lifecycle operations across a fleet. It does not run virtual machines.',
 'OME-Modular / MX9002m':'Chassis-management software and the module that runs it in MX7000. This is distinct from the sled’s iDRAC and from fabric switches.',
 'Mezzanine / IOM':'A mezzanine is an adapter in a compute sled. An I/O module provides chassis network / storage connectivity. The supported bay and fabric mapping matters.',
 'GPU / AI accelerator':'Hardware that speeds up specialized parallel work. NVIDIA and AMD GPUs and Intel Gaudi accelerators use their own software and interconnect ecosystems.',
 'HBM':'High-bandwidth memory attached to an accelerator. It is separate from host DDR5 and persistent SSD storage.',
 'SXM / OAM / HGX':'SXM and OAM are accelerator-module formats. NVIDIA HGX is an integrated GPU platform. These are not interchangeable with ordinary PCIe cards.',
 'NVLink / Infinity Fabric / RoCE':'Different interconnect technologies. Accelerator and cluster designs specify which is used; matching CPU brands do not make the links interchangeable.',
 'DLC / IR7000':'Direct liquid cooling removes heat through liquid-cooled components. IR7000 is Dell integrated-rack infrastructure for compatible systems such as XE9785L.',
 'Hypervisor / HCI':'A hypervisor runs virtual machines. Hyperconverged infrastructure combines compute and software-defined storage under a separately validated solution.'
};
const quiz=[
 {q:'What does the “17G” PowerEdge label describe?',options:['A server with seventeen CPU cores.','Dell’s server generation.','The GPU generation.'],answer:1,why:'Dell’s platform generation is separate from the processor family. These 17G rack examples use Xeon 6 or EPYC 9005.',src:'portfolio'},
 {q:'Which pair compares single-socket AMD in 1U and 2U?',options:['R670 and R770','R6715 and R7715','R6725 and R7725'],answer:1,why:'R6715 is 1U / one socket; R7715 is 2U / one socket. R6725 and R7725 are dual-socket AMD designs.',src:'rack'},
 {q:'Can an Intel CPU host AMD Instinct accelerators?',options:['Yes, in a specifically qualified platform.','No, CPU and GPU brands must match.','Only in a tower server.'],answer:0,why:'XE9680 combines Intel Xeon host CPUs with separate qualified NVIDIA, AMD MI300X or Intel Gaudi 3 builds. CPU brand is not a GPU compatibility rule.',src:'xe9680'},
 {q:'What does OME-Modular manage in an MX system?',options:['Only the guest virtual machines.','Only GPU memory.','The chassis and its compute, I/O, power and cooling resources.'],answer:2,why:'OME-Modular runs on MX9002m management modules. Sleds also have their own iDRAC. Workload traffic uses the fabric I/O modules.',src:'omem'},
 {q:'What does “E3.S NVMe” describe?',options:['Two names for a RAID level.','A physical SSD form factor and a storage protocol.','A fixed drive capacity.'],answer:1,why:'E3.S is the shape; NVMe is the protocol. The chassis and storage configuration must qualify both.',src:'rack'},
 {q:'What is the usual role of Dell BOSS?',options:['Dedicated boot storage, often using a mirrored M.2 pair.','Combining all GPU memory automatically.','Switching the workload network.'],answer:0,why:'BOSS separates boot storage from the main data bays. The exact device, RAID modes and drive options vary by PowerEdge model.',src:'mx760'},
 {q:'Can XE9785L be treated as an ordinary 3U rack server?',options:['Yes, OU and U are identical.','Yes, if the CPU is AMD.','No, it is a 3-OU node for compatible IR7000 infrastructure.'],answer:2,why:'Open Rack Units differ from conventional rack units. XE9785L also needs the appropriate rack power and direct-liquid-cooling infrastructure.',src:'xe9785l'},
 {q:'Can you combine a server’s maximum drive count and maximum GPU count automatically?',options:['Yes, every advertised maximum is simultaneous.','No, maxima can require different builds.','Only if iDRAC is installed.'],answer:1,why:'Drive cages, risers, CPU population, power and cooling compete for chassis resources. Read the exact model’s population and thermal rules.',src:'r770'}
];

